#!/bin/rc
# c++ — the APE C++ compiler driver.  One line, because the driver itself
# is `rc/bin/ape/eccp' and this is the POSIX-shaped name for it.
#
# THIS FILE USED TO BE THE CFRONT DRIVER, 420 lines of a three-stage
# pipeline (`pcc -E' -> `ns_strip' -> `cfront'), and cfront has been
# removed from the tree.  What replaced it is EDG's C-generating front
# end: `cpfe' translates C++ to C, `cc' compiles it, and `libedg.a' is
# the ABI runtime.  `eccp' is upstream's own name for that front end and
# holds the whole implementation, including the four things in it that
# are load-bearing and were each measured; read its header before
# changing anything here.
#
# TWO NAMES AND ONE IMPLEMENTATION, which is the only arrangement that
# cannot drift.  `c++' is what autoconf probes for, what GNU make
# defaults `CXX' to, and what `sys/src/cmd/transpilers' sets -- so it has
# to exist; `eccp' is what the NOTE, the release notes and
# `sys/include/ape/c++/README' all name.  A forwarder costs one exec.
#
# `$*' AND NOT `$"*'.  rc's `$*' passes the argument LIST through
# element by element, where `$"*' would flatten it into one string and a
# path containing a space would arrive as two arguments.  No file in this
# tree has one, which is exactly why it is written down rather than left
# to be discovered by the first one that does.

exec eccp $*
